+/// Which half of the overlay a draw call is responsible for.
+///
+/// The overlay is composited into the same ImGui draw list as the CEF pages, so
+/// the ORDER of the two calls is the layering: whatever is queued first is
+/// underneath. That order is not the same for every style, which is why this is
+/// an argument rather than a detail of `Draw`.
+///
+///   * A **screen** is a rectangle that exists in the world -- a television. It
+///     belongs UNDER the pages, so opening the freeroam menu covers the picture
+///     instead of the picture covering the menu. It used to be drawn after the
+///     pages, and a spawned television then painted over the whole menu.
+///   * A **label, card, ring or dot** is an annotation OF the world drawn for the
+///     player: a marker, a nameplate, a distance. Those want to be read, so they
+///     sit above the pages exactly as before.
+///
+/// `Draw` defaults to `Annotations` so every existing producer keeps the
+/// layering it was written against, and only a caller that knows it has screens
+/// on this frame asks for the other half.
+enum class Layer : uint8_t
+{
+    Screens,
+    Annotations,
+};
